{"In SpanFlusher.main, the 'produce' timer and 'segment_size_bytes' use tag key 'shard' while 'wait_produce' uses 'shards' for the same shard_tag value, splitting metrics by tag schema and preventing consistent per-shard querying": 0.9354526400566101, "SpanFlusher.join stops iterating over flusher processes when the timeout deadline is exceeded, so remaining processes are neither waited for nor terminated, potentially leaving child flushers running after shutdown/rebalance and leaking resources": 0.9637106657028198, "SpanFlusher creates a SpansBuffer per worker containing only that worker's shard subset, so SpansBuffer.flush_segments computes max_segments_per_shard from the subset size and can flush up to spans.buffer.max-flush-segments per process rather than per consumer, breaking the global flush cap and weakening the backpressure signal": 0.7859939336776733, "--flusher-processes accepts negative integers and SpanFlusher uses the value to size process_to_shards_map and compute i % self.num_processes, which then indexes a dict that has no corresponding keys, causing the consumer to crash on startup with a bad CLI value": 0.8364702463150024}